INSERT INTO `#__articles` (`article_id`, `category`, `title`, `name`, `banner`, `content`, `is_published`, `created_by`, `modified_by`, `created_at`, `modified_at`) VALUES
('1','News','Reservation Procedure','reservation-procedure','<h2>PROPERTY RESERVATION PROCEDURE</h2><p><em>Youâ€™ve made your decision to invest on your property. Now, allow us to guide you through the process and requirements to make your choice become truly yours.</em></p><p><br></p><h2><strong style="color: rgb(204, 204, 204);"><em>STEP 1</em></strong></h2><p><strong>SELECT &amp; CHOOSE.</strong></p><p>You may now choose which unit you wish to purchase. Your Property Specialist (PS) / Broker will verify the availability of your desired unit. Once it was confirmed that it is still available, you may now make an official reservation.</p><p><br></p><h2><strong style="color: rgb(204, 204, 204);"><em>STEP 2</em></strong></h2><p><strong>REVIEW.</strong></p><p>The PS will prepare a Computation Sheet that details the payment scheme that will be suitable for your home/investment purchase. Study financing options available and understand the legal and documentary requirements.</p><p><br></p><h2><strong style="color: rgb(204, 204, 204);"><em>STEP 3</em></strong></h2><p><strong>RESERVE &amp; PURCHASE.</strong></p><p>Once you have decided on the payment terms, your PS will help you accomplish your Reservation Agreement (RA) and Buyer"s Information Sheet (BIS). Your PS will assist you with the payment of your Reservation Fee (RF), which is valid for only 30 days. A receipt will be issued to you upon payment (Official, if Cash or Provisional if cheque).</p><p><br></p><h2><strong style="color: rgb(204, 204, 204);"><em>STEP 4</em></strong></h2><p><strong>DOCUMENTATION.</strong></p><ul><li>2 Valid Government Issued IDâ€™s with picture &amp; specimen like Passport, Driverâ€™s License, Postal ID, Company ID, etc</li><li>Photocopy of proof of billing from utility companies; water, phone, electric, etc.</li><li>Tax Identification Number (TIN)/ Accomplished BIR 1904 Form</li><li>Post Dated Checks (PDCs) that will cover the monthly downpayment &amp; 1 Guaranteed Check for the Balance.</li></ul><p><br></p>','1','Emanuel Florendo','Emanuel Florendo','1548388765','1548388765'),
('2','News','Careers at Philproperties','careers-at-philproperties','<p><a href="https://www.philproperties.ph/contact-us" class="btn btn-primary">Contact Us Now and Start Learning</a></p><ul>	<li><a href="#whysales">Why Sales?</a></li>	<li><a href="#whyrealestate">Why Real Estate?</a></li>	<li><a href="#whyphilproperties">Why Philproperties?</a></li></ul><br/><h2><a name="whysales">WHY SALES?</a></h2><p>First of all, it breaks the monotony of a 9 to 6 job. Being in sales lets you take control of your time and do things at your own pace. Sales also give you the freedom to work the way you want to work. It gives you freedom to express yourself your way.</p><p>It is also a career path wherein risks are low and the rewards can be as high as you want. The harder you work, the more rewards you earn therefore personal gratification is reinforced which in turn gives you more confidence in what you do.</p><p>And lastly, youâ€™ll find yourself enjoying being in sales, that is if you like meeting new people and seeing different places.</p><p><br></p><h2><strong><a name="whyrealestate">WHY REAL ESTATE?</a></strong></h2><p>We all know that it is a basic need for each and every one of us which means that it is something that will always be in demand. For us Filipinos, owning a piece of property is a sign of stability, a person or a family is on its way up.</p><p>We also know that real estate isnâ€™t exactly an unlimited thing. This is where the Law of Supply and Demand comes in. If the demand for real estate is higher than its supply, the prices of real estate increase. This is the main reason why properties appreciate in value as time passes. This is also why real estate is what most multi-millionaires tend to invest on; it is a measure of wealth. Real estate is also a good hedge for inflation and a good source of passive income.</p><p><br></p><h2><strong><a name="whyphilproperties">WHY PHILPROPERTIES?</a></strong></h2><p>Why should you join Philproperties? As mentioned, the Philippines has a wide range of developers putting up different projects around the Metro. What does this have to do with Philproperties? Philproperties International Corporation is accredited with most of these developers giving PPIC authority to sell all these projects. This inventory of over a billion pesos worth is available to all Philproperties sales persons which in turn provide them with more than enough projects to offer their clients.</p><p>Philproperties also provides competitive and progressive professional rates which means there is ample room for growth. In line with growth, continuous professional education seminars as well as different trainings are also provided to all who are affiliated with PPIC.</p><p>PPIC also provide staff support and constant updates about the different projects which eliminates the hassle of going the different developer offices to get them yourself. This make you work and manage your time more efficiently.</p><p>Another tool that will make you work more efficiently is our CRM or the Customer Relations Management. This system lets you organize everything related to your real estate selling like contact details of prospects, different projects you offer, and it even lets you forward files or send emails to your clients. And lastly PPIC also offers customized websites for more exposure and to project professionalism and credibility.</p><p><a href="https://www.philproperties.ph/contact-us" class="btn btn-primary">Contact Us Now and Start Learning</a></p>','1','Emanuel Florendo','Emanuel Florendo','1548389286','1548389286'),
('3','News','RESA will professionalize industry, says expert','resa-will-professionalize-industry-says-expert','<p>MANILA, Philippines - The new Real Estate Service Act of the Philippines, Republic Act No. 9646 (RESA), will professionalize 30,000 practitioners in the country and develop a corps of competent consultants, appraisers, brokers and assessors, both private and public, who can maximize the potentials of the industry.</p><p>This was the pronouncement of Dr. Eduardo G. Ong, chairman of the Professional Regulatory Board of Real Estate Service (PRB-RES) of the Professional Regulation Commission (PRC), during the recent Chamber of Real Estate and Builders Association (CREBA) general membership meeting.</p><p>Also during the meeting, CREBA, led by its national president, Jun Dulalia, launched its first International Convention to be held in Macau on October 26 &amp; 27, 2010 and signed two (memorandum of agreements with Pag-IBIG on Social Housing Program and with Metro Manila Development Authority (MMDA) on a cable television tie-up regarding real estate.</p><p>RESA created the PRB-RES, composed of a chairperson and four members appointed by the President of the Philippines, under the administration of the PRC, to supervise and regulate the registration, licensure and practice of real estate service in the country.</p><p>Hence, the board will conduct the licensure examinations for practitioners and issue, suspend, revoke or reinstate certificates of registration or professional identification cards. It will likewise maintain a register of licensed professionals, monitor their practices and adopt a national Code of Ethics and Responsibilities for the sector.</p><p>Except for real estate sales people, Filipinos who want to be registered and licensed as real estate service practitioners must take an examination which the board will give at least once every year in places and dates that the PRC will designate. In addition, all real estate brokers and private real estate appraisers shall be required to post a professional indemnity insurance, cash or surety bond, renewable every three years, for at least P20,000.</p><p>Local schools will be offering a Bachelor of Science in Real Estate starting school year 2011-2012. The board, in cooperation with the Commission on Higher Education (CHED) and concerned state universities and colleges, will prescribe the curricula for academic courses in real estate service.</p><p>Violators of the law will be slapped with a P100,000 fine or two years imprisonment, or both, according to Ong.</p><p>"The RESA will provide opportunities for real estate practitioners to be called professionals and practice in other countries although the law is not as perfect as it should be," he added.</p><p>At present, the PRB-RES is conducting consultations and public hearings about the Imple.</p><p><br></p><p>Philippine Star</p><p>June 11, 2010</p>','1','Emanuel Florendo','Emanuel Florendo','1549485831','1549485831'),
('4','News','More than 100,000 real estate agents and brokers affected by the new RESA law','more-than-100000-real-estate-agents-and-brokers-affected-by-the-new-resa-law','<p>AFTER nearly 22 years, real estate service practitioners in the Philippines will be professionalized and will have to get licenses from the Professional Regulatory Commission, as the Real Estate Service Act took effect Thursday.</p><p>The Real Estate Service Act of the Philippines, which aims to "safeguard and protect legitimate licensed real estate service practitioners,â€ will lead to the creation of a Bachelor of Science in Real Estate Service, which should be recognized by the Commission on Higher Education and the Professional Regulatory Board on Real Estate Service.</p><p>"to finally and completely eradicate the pernicious practices of unauthorized or unlicensed individuals,â€ the new law, Republic Act 9646, said.</p><p>The provision serves as an additional security for the public when transacting with brokers or appraisers. Under the new law, real estate consultants, appraisers, local government assessors and brokers will be overseen by the Professional Regulatory Board of Real Estate Service under the PRC.</p><p>Under the bill, which will affected more or less than 100, 000 agents and brokers, the Professional Regulation Commission will take over from the Department of Trade and Industry in administering examinations for real estate service practitioners in the private sector.</p><p>Unlicensed practitioners for real estate will be meted with a penalty ranging P200,000 to P2,000,000, as well as 1year to 12 years imprisonment.</p><p>CHED executive director Atty. Julito Vitriolo said there are several schools offering such courses on real estate, as he expects them to grow further. "I think with the passage of this bill, more schools will seek accreditation for courses on real estate,â€ he said. They will be subjected to a licensing process that will require them to pass a technical examination, comply with the program of continuing education and training, and observe the Code of Conduct and Responsibilities.</p><p>Salespersons, although not considered part of the professional group, will be accredited by the PRC, after undergoing training and working under a licensed real estate broker. RESA will require real estate practitioners to post a Professional Indemnity Insurance/Cash or Surety Bond upon taking their oath to practice the profession before the PRC.</p><p>The new law is expected to stimulate the property market, encourage investments in construction and development, generate employment and increase revenues for the government.</p><p>The bill also includes a provision requiring a professional indemnity insurance/cash or surety bond for real estate brokers and private appraisers. The bill sets the minimum limit at only P20,000 but the client is free to impose additional requirements depending on the transaction involved. The provision serves as an additional security for the public when transacting with brokers or appraisers.</p><p>It was sponsored in the House by Iloilo City Representative Rep. Raul T. Gonzalez Jr., chair of the Committee on Civil Service and Professional Regulation, and in the Senate by Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson, acting chair of the Committee on Civil Service and Government Reorganization.</p><p>The law, according to Senate President Juan Ponce Enrile, should protect the public from unscrupulous real estate service practitioners.</p><p>Manny Florendo of Philproperties lauded the passage of the law, adding that real estate service practitioners are helping ensure the vibrant movement of capital to support economic activities that would generate more resources for development projects.</p><p>"It is just right that the real estate practice should be regulated through appropriate licensing and the observance of a code of ethics with a defined disciplinary procedure for the protection of the public,â€ Florendo said.</p><p>Real estate service practitioners include real estate consultants, appraisers, assessors, brokers and salespersons. But the bill will require only real estate consultants, appraisers, assessors and brokers to have licenses and other requirements.</p><p>To help these agents and brokers, Florendo said their company- Philproperties Corporation are open to assist affected agents in getting their licenses under the new implementing guidelines.</p><p>Philproperties is also extending their arms to the newly licensed brokers to help them in starting their career ...</p><p>"Just contact us at phone number 287-3128, or cellphone number 0917.830.7742", Florendo said.</p>','1','Emanuel Florendo','Emanuel Florendo','1549485928','1549485928'),
('5','News','Does a Real Estate Sales Person need a License to Market Properties in the Philippines?','does-a-real-estate-sales-person-need-a-license-to-market-properties-in-the-philippines','<p>The answer to that is yes the RESA law is prohibiting unlicensed Sales Person to sell properties that they donâ€™t own and no if they lawfully own the property that they are selling, a trustee or assignee in bankruptcy or insolvency proceedings and any person acting pursuant to the order of any court of justice are also exempted to this law.</p><p>To those people who want to be a part of real estate selling and to those who are already selling but are not yet licensed you must take note of this. The RESA Law or the Real Estate Service Act of the Philippines aims to "safeguard and protect legitimate licensed real estate service practitioners, to finally and completely eradicate the pernicious practices of unauthorized or unlicensed individuals and lastly as an additional security for the public when transacting with brokers or appraisers. Under the bill unlicensed practitioners for real estate will be meted with a penalty ranging P200,000 to P2,000,000, as well as 1 year to 12 years imprisonment.</p>','1','Emanuel Florendo','Emanuel Florendo','1549486196','1549486196'),
('6','News','Advantages of being accredited with Philproperties International Corporation (PPIC)','advantages-of-being-accredited-with-philproperties-international-corporation-ppic','<p>PPIC provides updates for all projects from all developers to lessen the hassle that you might go through without a broker.</p><ul><li>PPIC provides leads to agents.</li><li>PPIC has billions worth of properties available to be offered to clients.</li><li>PPIC provides personal web pages to agents for easier listing and better web exposure</li><li>PPIC makes use of the CRM or Customer Relations Management system. This system provides all necessary documents and information with regards to sales transactions</li><li>PPIC provides helpful advice and guidance gathered from 20 years of experience in the industry.</li><li>The RESA law decrees that only Brokers and property owners can sell real estate. Being affiliated with Philproperties gives you legal authority to keep selling real estate listed under PPIC.</li><li>Agents will be able to sell more types of projects and properties which in turn boost the number of potential sales and earnings.</li><li>There is no pressure in meeting a quota every month.</li><li>Agents will be able to sell properties from different developers at the same time.</li><li>Commission rates are more competitive</li><li>Agents will be able to tap into a wider array of clients.</li><li>PPIC provides support in everything involved with closing a sale.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Since the RESA law is now implemented, being accredited with a broker is not just an advantage, it now a requirement since non-brokers cannot sell or practice Real Estate projects. And besides al these advantages, being affiliated with PPIC gives you access to all projects listed with the broker and the agent does not have to worry about the accreditation with the different developers. This is also a good step towards having a successful career in the real estate industry. This will also help should one decides to put up their own real estate firm.</p><p>To better your chances in being a successful real estate practitioner and for more information, visit www.philproperties.ph or contact us @ 287-3128.</p><p><br></p>','1','Emanuel Florendo','Emanuel Florendo','1549486303','1549486303'),
('7','News','A conducive work environment makes for a productive worker','a-conducive-work-environment-makes-for-a-productive-worker','<p>Experienced and successful salespersons such as brokers and agents recognize and appreciate a productive work environment conducive for maximizing earning potentials.&nbsp;</p><p>Philproperties International Corporation provides systems which makes it easier for salespersons to produce on a higher level. One of these systems is what we call CRM or Customer Relations Management. It is an online system that acts as a salespersonâ€™s organizer. Philproperties also provides regular updates from all our listed developers. This lessens the salespersonâ€™s work load therefore giving him more time to concentrate on different aspects of the business. And lastly, Philproperties provide competitive commission rates to loyal salespersons.</p><p>At Philproperties, we donâ€™t only provide quality projects and services to clientsâ€¦ we also provide ample opportunity and motivation to our sales force.&nbsp;</p>','1','Emanuel Florendo','Emanuel Florendo','1549486465','1549486465'),
('8','News','Advantages of being a Real Estate Practitioner','advantages-of-being-a-real-estate-practitioner','<p>There are a few businesses that offer the same type of freedom, compensation, and fulfillment that real estate provides. In real estate, one is in charge of his/ her own time and the compensation is directly in relation to how much one works. This in turn gives a great deal of sense of fulfillment and achievement.</p><p>At Philproperties International Corporation, our sales force enjoy all these factors for the reason that sales are not quota based which means there is less pressure on the salesperson to maintain a steady number of closed sales. Philproperties also provides competitive commission rates and incentives which in turn motivate the sales force to work better.</p><p>If you think you want to be a part of this corporation and be successful in real estate, why not reply to this message and we can an appointment to discuss this further.</p>','1','Emanuel Florendo','Emanuel Florendo','1549486495','1549486495'),
('9','News','What is CRM?','what-is-crm','<p>Customer Relations Management (CRM) is a widely implemented model for managing a company"s interactions with customers, clients, and sales prospects. It involves using technology to organize, automate, and synchronize business processesâ€”principally sales activities, but also those for marketing, customer service, and technical support.</p><p>True CRM brings together information from all data sources within an organization (and where appropriate, from outside the organization) to give one, holistic view of each customer in real time. This allows customer facing employees in such areas as sales, customer support, and marketing to make quick yet informed decisions on everything from cross-selling and up selling opportunities to target marketing strategies to competitive positioning tactics.</p><p>What a CRM will do for your Business</p><p>A properly implemented CRM should:</p><ol><li>Store information about leads, opportunities and customers so that all the people involved stay informed</li><li>Act as a central shared system for contacts, calendars and files</li><li>Use reminders to make sure that you never leave a prospect behind</li><li>Determine the effectiveness of marketing, industry segments or pretty much anything else</li><li>Integrate into your existing workflow</li><li>Reduce administration costs</li></ol><p><br></p><p>Here at Philproperties, the CRM system is one of our main tools in our daily activities in real estate. Whether it be recording contacts and their details, sending documents and information to clients, storing projects and listing, and just basically organizing everything that has to do with real estate transactions.</p><p>If you want to know more about our CRM system, we are inviting you to attend our<strong> REAL ESTATE BUSINESS OPPORTUNITY SESSION</strong> here in our office at unit 932 City and Land Megaplaza, ADB Ave, corner Garnett Rd. Ortigas Center, Pasig.</p><p><br></p>','1','Emanuel Florendo','Emanuel Florendo','1549486699','1549486699'),
('10','News','Be A Successful Real Estate Practitioner','be-a-successful-real-estate-practitioner','<p>There are a few factors that are essential to being successful in real estate. One is knowing which type of property to sell, another is a conducive work environment and last is proper motivation.</p><p>As a conscious and ongoing effort to meet these factors, Philproperties have been hard at work in getting accreditation with most of the leading developers in the country providing a variety of available projects. Also, PPIC has tie-ups with different banks which adds foreclosed property to our inventory. This gives our sales persons diversity in the types of property available for them to market.</p><p>Philproperties work environment puts emphasis on the salesperson"s maximization of time and earning potential and motivation. This is done by providing them with CRM, an online Customer Relation Management system and by providing competitive commission rates and incentives.</p><p>If you think that you can be successful in real estate or if you need a new environment, we would appreciate your response to this letter and maybe set a time and date for a meeting so we can discuss this subject further.</p>','1','Emanuel Florendo','Emanuel Florendo','1549486862','1549486862'),
('11','News','Real Estate Online Band Wagon!','real-estate-online-band-wagon','<p>These days, people have been so busy with their hectic schedules that the aid of technology, the internet to be more specific, had become a necessity. It has even come to the point that more and more businesses are hopping on the internet band wagon and operate online. This is the trend that our company strives to flourish on. Philproperties International Corporation is a professional online real estate marketing company which has been providing not only excellent projects and services to clients but competitive compensation rates and incentives to our sales force.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>If you are in the real estate business or want to be in it, Philproperties International Corporation is a company that will welcome and provide you with the tools that will help you on your way to success.</p>','1','Emanuel Florendo','Emanuel Florendo','1549486908','1549486908'),
('12','News','2 Ways to Make More Money in Real Estate','2-ways-to-make-more-money-in-real-estate','<p>There are two ways to make more money in real estate. 1st is to sell more property and the other is to reduce costs. At Philproperties International Corporation, we help you with both ways. With accreditation with most of the leading developers in the Philippines, Philproperties has over 500,000,000 worth of inventory. Available at your disposal are different types of condos, townhouses, foreclosed property, house &amp;lots and the like. Philproperties also provides brokers and gents systems and services that would lessen their operational costs thus widening their profit margin. At Philproperties, we make sure that we maximize every project"s profitability.</p><p>If you are interested in increasing your earnings, email us at info@philproperties.ph or call 287-3128.</p><p>We are looking forward to working with you!</p>','1','Emanuel Florendo','Emanuel Florendo','1549487067','1549487067'),
('13','News','4 Whys in Real Estate','4-whys-in-real-estate','<p>4 Why"s: Why Sales? Why Real Estate? Why the Philippines? Why Philproperties?</p><p>Sales... Why should get into sales? First of all, it breaks the monotony of a 9 to six job. Being in sales lets you take control of your time and do things at your own pace. Sales also give you the freedom to work the way you want to work. It gives you freedom to express yourself your way. It is also a career path wherein risks are low and the rewards can be as high as you want. The harder you work, the more rewards you earn therefore personal gratification is reinforced which in turn gives you more confidence in what you do. And lastly, you"ll find yourself enjoying being in sales, that is if you like meeting new people and seeing different places.</p><p>Real Estate... Why should you get in to real estate? We all know that it is a basic need for each and every one of us which means that it is something that will always be in demand. And we also know that real estate isn"t exactly an unlimited thing. This is where the Law of Supply and Demand comes in. If the demand for real estate is higher than its supply, the prices of real estate increase. This is the main reason why properties appreciate in value as time passes. This is also why real estate is what most multi-millionaires tend to invest on; it is a measure of wealth.&nbsp;Real estate is also a good hedge for inflation and a good source of passive income.</p><p>The Philippines... Why should you invest on real estate in the Philippines? The current status of the industry here is booming. With a wide variety of developers putting up different projects almost everywhere in the Metro, buyers now have a bigger range to choose from. Real estate prices in Metro Manila are also considerably lower compared to the prices from the other major cities in Asia. But this does not mean that the properties here are subpar compared to the projects abroad. Developers here now follow strict international standards in building structures and use international concepts which reassure you that you are investing in something of good quality.</p><p>Philproperties... Why should you join Philproperties? I mentioned previously that the Philippines has a wide range of developers putting up different projects around the Metro. What does this have to do with Philproperties? Philproperties International Corporation is accredited with most of these developers giving PPIC authority to sell all these projects. This inventory of over a billion pesos worth is available to all Philproperties sales persons which in turn provide them with more than enough projects to offer their clients. Philproperties also provides competitive and progressive professional rates which means there is ample room for growth. In line with growth, continuous professional education seminars as well as different trainings are also provided to all who are affiliated with PPIC. PPIC also provide staff support and constant updates about the different projects which eliminates the hassle of going the different developer offices to get them yourself. This make you work and manage your time more efficiently. Another tool that will make you work more efficiently is our CRM or the Customer Relations Management. This system lets you organize everything related to your real estate selling like contact details of prospects, different projects you offer, and it even lets you forward files or send emails to your clients. And lastly PPIC also offers customized websites for more exposure and to project professionalism and credibility.</p>','1','Emanuel Florendo','Emanuel Florendo','1549487211','1549487211'),
('14','News','Helpful Tips for First time Real Estate Buyer','helpful-tips-for-first-time-real-estate-buyer','<p>When buying new property, it is important to look for properties backed by established developers and licensed real estate agents/ brokers, especially in cases of off-plan or pre-selling (the property is at the planning stages and non-existent during the time of the sale).</p><p>In general, property can be acquired by simple agreement. After deciding what property to buy as well as inspecting the premises and documents, the buyer usually signs a binding notarized Deed of Sale. Employing the services of a reputable sales agent is convenient because they not only provide vital information regarding the transaction and property, but also assist the buyer in getting the best quality property that they should have but rather give them the best service that they can give.</p>','1','Emanuel Florendo','Emanuel Florendo','1549487254','1549487254'),
('15','News','10 Reasons Why "Now" Is the Best Time to Buy Real Estate in the Philippines','10-reasons-why-now-is-the-best-time-to-buy-real-estate-in-the-philippines','<p>I have been in the real estate business for more than 20 years. During my day-to-day meetings with my friends and clients, I was often asked about the situation of buying and selling real estate in the Philippines. Understandably, because almost every day we are hearing negative news about the world economy, lay-offs, retrenchment, and the offer of early retirement packages.</p><p>This was their usual questions, "during this time of pandemic is it the right time to buy properties in the Philippines?". My answers were always -" YES, of course !". Below are my the reasons WHY :</p><ol><li>Prices and terms of payments in buying real estate nowadays are very flexible.</li><li>At present, developers and sellers of real estate properties are very cooperative.</li><li>Financial institutions such as PAG-IBIG and banks are much willing to lend money.</li><li>Interest rates now in acquiring Philippine properties have never been this good.</li><li>The sellers are willing to take less than the value of their properties.</li><li>Baka magastos mo money mo. You might not be able to have the opportunity to buy your dream house and lot.</li><li>Kapag hindi ka bumili ngayon , Ibig sabihin , matagal ka pa na magre-rent.</li><li>Matagal ka pang makikisama sa landlord o sa neighbour mo.</li><li>Or makikisama sa Biyenan , Hipag, O bayaw nyo</li><li>At Lagi ka na lang mangangarap na mag-karoon ng sarili mong bahay.</li></ol><p><br></p><p>If you are thinking of owning a property visit www.philproperties.ph or send a message to 0917-8307742 for free home buying consultation. </p>','1','Emanuel Florendo','Emanuel Florendo','1549487482','1549487482'),
('16','News','Practical Tips For Buying A Piece of Real Estate','practical-tips-for-buying-a-piece-of-real-estate','<p><strong><em>     </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>     Shopping for a new home is a very exciting and emotional experience and it is because of this that it is very easy to lose track of your main objective in buying a home. One should always keep in mind that is also quite an important transaction given that you"re pretty much dealing with one of our most basic needs and most probably your biggest investment. Getting carried away by all the excitement may lead to a very costly mistake. It"s ether you pay a whole lot more that what it"s actually worth, buy the wrong property, or worse, lose the property you"re eying.</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>     Such mistakes are hard to avoid especially if you"re inexperienced in acquiring a piece of real estate and more often than not, you will realize that you already have when it is already too late. To avoid having to go through such ordeals, here are some tips that would help you make buying your new home a relatively easy and positive experience as it should be.</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>     First, Research. Gathering all relevant information is crucial if you don"t want to put out a ridiculously high offer or miss out on a great deal. Seeking assistance from a trusted, professional real estate broker with a good track record and experience may be all the difference between owning your dream home or settling with a property that"s 2nd choice.&nbsp;A broker"s in depth knowledge and experience in the field may offer a basis of objective and sound advice.     </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>     Knowing what you really need. Having a mere idea of what you really want for a home or any kind of property is not enough. This will only make your decision making tougher. In buying a property, you should always know what you"re looking for and just stick with what you really need initially. </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>     Information such as land area, floor area, property type, features &amp;amp; amenities and location are a few of the factors you should really be decided on even before starting to shop. Also, while shopping for a piece of real estate, having a practical and objective frame of mind will go a long way in terms of avoiding overspending.    </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Checking the title of the property will guarantee you that you are buying a legitimate property without any debts tied to it. A realtor can provide you a copy of the title and other documentations that will ensure you that there are no liens, undisclosed owners, leasers or easements against the title.</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>     Acquire an updated survey. This is a report that will provide you with information regarding boundaries and structural changes within your property such as a swimming pool, or your neighbor"s fence crossing boundary lines. This will guarantee that you are getting what you pay for.</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>     Brace yourself and minimize the unexpected. It is advisable at this stage to hire a professional inspector to conduct a complete and thorough inspection of the property. This can mean the difference between buying a good quality property or a property with major faults that are not usually obvious to the untrained eye.     </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>     Find out or at least have an estimate of all fees and taxes to be paid in the near future so as not to be found surprised by a huge bill for such fees. </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>     Knowing the history of the property such as previous repairs monthly dues and taxes will give you a better idea of how much more you"ll be spending for your property.</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>     Be one step ahead. Getting financing pre-approval gives a buyer more credibility and is more likely to be considered as a serious buyer. This will help make the transaction go smother plus it makes you be on the offensive side of the transaction.</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>     Lastly, never rush. Before putting your John Hancock on the dotted line, make sure that you understand all conditions and stipulations within your transaction. This is to avoid any kind of problems in the process.     </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>     These are all the little things you have to keep in mind whenever buying a piece of land. Nowadays, there are a number of brokers that are willing to help you. One of which is Philproperties International Corporation, a professional online real estate company that cater to Filipinos who are looking to acquire a piece of land from their home land.</em></strong></p>','1','Emanuel Florendo','Emanuel Florendo','1549487591','1549487591'),
('17','News','Processes in Investing on a Real Estate Property','processes-in-investing-on-a-real-estate-property','<p><strong>For your guidance, here are the standard steps in purchasing a real estate property:</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li>INQUIRY. This is when the client expresses interest in a project.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>SETTING OF TRIPPING This is when the salesperson orients the client and shows him/her around the project.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>RESERVATION: Once the client decides on which project he/she likes, he/she pays the reservation fee to hold the particular unit.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>DOWNPAYMENT: This is when the buyer pays his initial investment to the seller.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>CONTRACT SIGNING: Here is when the buyer sign the agreement and  issue PDC"s if required by the seller.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>SUBMISSION OF REQUIRED DOCUMENT: This includes the Contract to Sell, Identification Cards, Proof billings, Photos, etc.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>PROCESSING OF FINANCING: Buyer fill-up the bank loan application form. The buyer should start accomplishing the required docs for bank financing after the Reservation. These include the proof of income, pay slips, income tax return, financial statement, IDs, </li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>TRANSFER OF TITLE: Should the client opt to pay through bank financing, the title of the property will remain in the possession of the bank until the full amount has been paid.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>MOVE-IN. This is after the seller turn-over the unit to the buyer.</li></ul><p><br></p>','1','Emanuel Florendo','Emanuel Florendo','1549487678','1549487678'),
('18','News','Navigating Land Title Transfer Fees in the Philippines.','navigating-land-title-transfer-fees-in-the-philippines','<p>Navigating Land Title Transfer Fees in the Philippines<br /><br />Transferring land titles, be it a certificate of title or a condominium certificate of title, in the Philippines involves a multifaceted array of fees. While the conventional approach dictates shared responsibility between sellers and buyers, flexible arrangements can be negotiated, provided they are mutually agreed upon before the signing of the Deed of Sale.</p><p>Unraveling the Standard Procedures for Fees:<br />Capital Gains Tax (CGT):<br />Sellers bear the responsibility for the Capital Gains Tax, a fixed 6% of the total contract price or the selling price stated in the Deed of Sale, opting for the higher amount. For sellers who are corporations or actively engage in real estate selling, Withholding Tax applies. Additionally, sellers must settle any outstanding real estate taxes and cover the commission of the licensed real estate broker or brokerage agency facilitating the transaction.</p><p>Buyer"s Responsibilities:<br />Documentary Tax (1.5%):<br />Buyers are tasked with shouldering the Documentary Tax, equivalent to 1.5% of the selling price or zonal value, whichever is greater.</p><p>Transfer Tax (Location-Specific Rates):<br />Buyers are obligated to pay the Transfer Tax, with the exact percentage varying based on the property"s location. For properties in Metro Manila and key cities, specific rates apply, approximately ranging from 0.5% to 0.75%, offering a nuanced understanding of the financial commitment. In contrast, properties in provinces or municipalities have distinct rates, adding a layer of complexity to the overall transfer process.</p><p>Registration Fee (Property Value-Dependent):<br />The Registration Fee, calculated as a percentage of the property"s value, is within the buyer"s responsibilities. Notably, properties in Metro Manila and key cities carry different rates compared to those in provinces or municipalities. For instance, in Metro Manila, the registration fee is approximately 0.75% of the property"s value, emphasizing the need for location-specific insights.</p><p>Value Added Tax (VAT):<br />Rate: The Value Added Tax (VAT) is typically set at 12%.<br />Applicability: Buyers are generally responsible for the Value Added Tax. It applies to the sale of new residential properties and lots exceeding ?3,199,200.<br />Educational Fund Fee:<br />Rate: Usually around 1% of the property"s selling price.<br />Applicability: The Educational Fund Fee is a mandatory contribution to the Education Fund of the local government unit. Buyers are commonly responsible for this fee.<br />Business Tax:<br />Rate: Business Tax rates can vary based on the local government"s regulations.<br />Applicability: Business Tax, when applicable, is generally borne by the seller. It applies to transactions involving properties held for business purposes.<br />Notarial Fee:<br />Buyers cover the Notarial Fee, encompassing the legal documentation associated with the property transfer, ensuring a smooth transition of ownership.</p><p>Incidental and Miscellaneous Expenses:<br />Buyers are accountable for any additional incidental and miscellaneous expenses arising during the registration and transfer process, emphasizing the importance of thorough financial planning.</p><p>Agreements and Considerations:<br />Mutual Agreements:<br />While standard procedures exist, sellers and buyers retain the flexibility to mutually agree on alternative terms concerning fee distribution before finalizing the Deed of Sale. This allows for a personalized approach tailored to the specific circumstances of the transaction.</p><p>Disclaimers and Suggestions:<br />Consultation with Professionals:</p><p>The information provided is a general overview, and real estate transactions can be complex. It is strongly recommended that individuals consult with legal, tax, and real estate professionals to obtain personalized advice based on their specific situation.<br />Legal and Tax Implications:</p><p>Real estate transactions involve legal and tax implications that may vary based on individual circumstances. Professional advice can provide clarity on these aspects and ensure compliance with current regulations.<br />Location-Specific Guidance:</p><p>Rates and regulations can differ based on the location of the property. Seeking advice from professionals familiar with local laws and practices is essential for accurate and location-specific information.<br />By providing a detailed insight into transfer fee rates and registration fees, both in Metro Manila and key cities and in provinces or municipalities, this comprehensive guide aims to empower individuals navigating the complex landscape of land title transfers in the Philippines. Understanding the specific taxes and fees applicable to each transaction type enhances transparency and facilitates informed decision-making in real estate transactions.</p>','1','Emanuel Florendo','Emanuel Florendo','1549487814','1549487814'),
('21','News','Real Estate Industry in the Philippines Statistics and Facts','real-estate-industry-in-the-philippines-statistics-and-facts','<p><span style="color: rgb(69, 95, 124);">The real estate industry is a key driver of the Philippine economy, generating&nbsp;</span><a href="https://www.lamudi.com.ph/breathtaking-stylish-uk-inspired-interior-ready-to-168993186042.html" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 119, 213); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">gross value added</a><span style="color: rgb(69, 95, 124);">&nbsp;of nearly 529 billion Philippine pesos in 2021. Due to the growing middle-class population and the sustained remittances from overseas Filipino workers (OFWs), Filipinos" purchasing and investing power in real estate properties had been gradually increasing in recent years.</span></p><p><br></p><h2>Residential real estate in the Philippines</h2><p>Residential real estate in the Philippines comprises a wide range of residential properties, from public and private housing to mid-range subdivisions, condominiums, and high-class villages. In 2020, a survey revealed that&nbsp;<a href="https://www.lamudi.com.ph/breathtaking-stylish-uk-inspired-interior-ready-to-168993186042.html" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 119, 213);">most Filipino households live in a single-house unit</a>, with more than half owning the property or having an owner-like possession. For metropolitan cities like Metro Manila, renting apartments, purchasing rent-to-own units in subdivisions, and taking a lease in a condominium is quite common. The average selling price would depend on the area of the property, reaching as much as 220 thousand Philippine pesos per square meter for a condo unit.</p><p><br></p><p>However, the&nbsp;<a href="https://www.lamudi.com.ph/breathtaking-stylish-uk-inspired-interior-ready-to-168993186042.html" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 119, 213);">exodus of households from rural areas</a>&nbsp;left the demand for affordable housing at an all-time high. As a result, there has been a growing and constant demand for socialized and low-cost housing among low-income families. On top of that, the Philippines’ geographical location makes it susceptible to&nbsp;<a href="https://www.lamudi.com.ph/breathtaking-stylish-uk-inspired-interior-ready-to-168993186042.html" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 119, 213);">natural disasters</a>, further challenging the country’s housing situation. To address the housing gap, government agencies and the private sector adopted a resolution that would expedite the inventory of idle government lands and fast-track the development and release of socialized housing for the growing number of informal settlers.</p><p><br></p><h2>State of commercial real estate</h2><p>Commercial real estate, composed of office space, industrial, retail, and hospitality properties, is slowly recovering from the impacts of the COVID-19 pandemic.&nbsp;<a href="https://www.lamudi.com.ph/breathtaking-stylish-uk-inspired-interior-ready-to-168993186042.html" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 119, 213);">Office space demand</a>&nbsp;is dominated by the IT-BPM sector, although the Philippine offshore gaming operators (POGO) industry is expected to return in the coming months. The&nbsp;<a href="https://www.lamudi.com.ph/breathtaking-stylish-uk-inspired-interior-ready-to-168993186042.html" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 119, 213);">vacancy rate of office spaces</a>&nbsp;also shows improvements in the coming years as companies re-occupy office spaces.</p><p><br></p><p>Retail real estate has also shown improvements in the vacancy rate, especially in the cities of Taguig and Makati, where most shopping malls and retail outlets are located. Food, beverage, clothing, and apparel will continue to lead the country"s&nbsp;<a href="https://www.lamudi.com.ph/breathtaking-stylish-uk-inspired-interior-ready-to-168993186042.html" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 119, 213);">upcoming retail real estate supply</a>.&nbsp;<em>This text provides general information. Statista assumes no liability for the information given being complete or correct. Due to varying update cycles, statistics can display more up-to-date data than referenced in the text.</em></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Published by&nbsp;<a href="https://www.statista.com/aboutus/our-research-commitment" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 119, 213);">Statista Research Department</a>,&nbsp;Jan 12, 2023 Research by Luzette Qader</p>','1','Philproperties Int','Philproperties Int','1681950293','1681950293'),
('22','News','Demographics of the Philippines Statistics and Facts','demographics-of-the-philippines-statistics-and-facts','<p><span style="color: rgb(69, 95, 124);">With over 111 million people, the Philippines was among the&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(0, 119, 213); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">most populated countries in the Asia Pacific</span><span style="color: rgb(69, 95, 124);">, next to Japan. Deep-seated Catholic beliefs influenced the nation’s pro-life stance and aided the population boom. However, the country’s population reflected&nbsp;</span><a href="https://www.lamudi.com.ph/breathtaking-stylish-uk-inspired-interior-ready-to-168993186042.html" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 119, 213); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">sluggish growth in the past decade</a><span style="color: rgb(69, 95, 124);">&nbsp;as evidenced by the&nbsp;</span><a href="https://www.lamudi.com.ph/breathtaking-stylish-uk-inspired-interior-ready-to-168993186042.html" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 119, 213); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">declining fertility rates</a><span style="color: rgb(69, 95, 124);">&nbsp;partly due to the increased use of contraceptives and modern family planning methods.</span></p><p><br></p><h2>A young demographic</h2><p>The Philippines has a young population, with about 64 percent of people between the ages of 15 and 64 years. Meanwhile, over 30 percent are between zero to 14 years old. In 2019, the mean age of male household members was 37.68 years while female members had a mean age of 44.2 years. The country’s young people were seen to significantly contribute to the&nbsp;<a href="https://www.lamudi.com.ph/breathtaking-stylish-uk-inspired-interior-ready-to-168993186042.html" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 119, 213);">country’s economic recovery</a>&nbsp;after experiencing prolonged COVID-19-related lockdowns.</p><p><br></p><h2>Urbanization and migration</h2><p>Despite the slow growth, the&nbsp;<a href="https://www.statista.com/statistics/640612/asia-pacific-population-density-by-country/" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 119, 213);">country’s population density remains among the highest in the region</a>. However, the distribution of people was uneven as&nbsp;<a href="https://www.lamudi.com.ph/breathtaking-stylish-uk-inspired-interior-ready-to-168993186042.html" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 119, 213);">more Filipinos chose to live in urban areas</a>&nbsp;where work opportunities remain abundant. As of May 2020, the regions of CALABARZON and the National Capital Region (NCR) accounted for the&nbsp;<a href="https://www.lamudi.com.ph/breathtaking-stylish-uk-inspired-interior-ready-to-168993186042.html" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 119, 213);">highest number of inhabitants</a>&nbsp;nationwide. This, in turn, created an income disparity among major capitals. In addition, the country saw a growing slum community that has been an ongoing societal issue in major urban cities.</p><p><br></p><p>The slum areas in the Philippines have contributed to the global share of the slum population in Southeast Asia. Although the&nbsp;<a href="https://www.lamudi.com.ph/breathtaking-stylish-uk-inspired-interior-ready-to-168993186042.html" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 119, 213);">share of the urban population living in the slums fluctuated</a>, the lack of affordable housing and economic inequality continued to challenge the living conditions and the quality of life of those who can only afford to squat in slums.</p><p><br></p><p>In terms of migration, the country has developed an emigration culture, where one out of five Filipinos expressed desires to move abroad. The government also relies on this emigration culture and has positioned the country as the&nbsp;<a href="https://www.lamudi.com.ph/breathtaking-stylish-uk-inspired-interior-ready-to-168993186042.html" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 119, 213);">leading labor exporter from Asia-Pacific</a>.&nbsp;<em>This text provides general information. Statista assumes no liability for the information given being complete or correct. Due to varying update cycles, statistics can display more up-to-date data than referenced in the text.</em></p><p>Research by Luzette Qader</p><p><br></p><p>Published by&nbsp;<a href="https://www.statista.com/aboutus/our-research-commitment" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 119, 213);">Statista Research Department</a>,&nbsp;Jan 31, 2023</p><p><br></p>','1','Philproperties Int','Philproperties Int','1681952117','1681952117'),
('24','News','Philproperties Supports Indigents Scholarship Program','philproperties-supports-indigents-scholarship-program','<p>Emanuel &ldquo;Manny&rdquo; Florendo, President and Chairman of the</p><p>Philproperties International Corporation recently expressed its full support for the<br />scholarship program for indigents of Camarines Norte Vice Governor Joseph V.<br />Ascutia. Realtor Florendo conveyed his intention to the provincial executive at<br />the golfing event held last November 21, 2023, at the Valley Golf and Country<br />Club in Antipolo City. The proceeds of this event titled &ldquo;Golf Tournament for a<br />Cause,&rdquo; a project of the vice governor which was also supported by Florendo,<br />are for the benefit of the poor but deserving college students from the Province<br />of Camarines Norte.<br />Florendo said he believes that to ensure the success of laudable<br />projects such as this, there should be involvement from the private sector. &ldquo;Our<br />government leaders could initiate, but the success of any endeavor for the<br />betterment of the lives of the less privileged rests upon the collective and<br />the positive response from our people, especially from the business sector,&rdquo; said<br />the realtor.<br />He also emphasized the value of education and training as it was thru<br />this that he himself rose from humble beginnings as a child from a middle-income family<br />in the third-class municipality of Capalonga in Camarines Norte. Likewise,<br />Florendo lauded the initiatives of Vice Governor Ascutia in coming up with pro-<br />poor projects that are not dependent on government funds for their<br />implementation.</p>','1','Philproperties Int','Philproperties Int','1701617365','1701617365'),